From e243a12ee321deff9029788874d056d648755fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Faris Hijazi <theefaris@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:10:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fleet): highlight live sessions and archive ended worker
 runs

Fleet rows keep T3's order. A live external session now tints its row by
what it is doing: Needs input pulses in the warning color, Working breathes in
the info color, Idle holds a static success tint, and Offline has none. Both
animations are the existing stepped status animations and stop under reduced
motion.

Discovery records which unattended worker (a scheduled routine or delegated
task) a session is a run of. When such a run ends, discovery archives its
thread once, so routine runs stop flooding the list while their history stays
in the archive. Unarchiving one is left alone.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_20cc9c1a6a80484ca54b4895500b171c
